# Dirtree: Stateful directory trees in the CLI for humans and LLMs. https://github.com/pmarreck/dirtree
ver=1.2
annotate=[
	build = nix build wrapper -> zig-out/bin. --debug/--test switch optimize mode.
	ceremony-preflight = Key-ceremony preflight: host checks, residual assumptions, --rehearse runs the whole tooling path on TEST keys through openssl/poppler/zbar oracles
	cli/main.c = The CLI, in C on purpose: C cannot @import the Zig core, so bypassing the FFI is inexpressible rather than merely discouraged.
	docs/CUSTODY_AND_ISSUER_API_V1.md = DRAFT key custody (hot Worker secret + cold sigil keyfile from one seed), ceremony script, issuer/confirmation API bounds, rotation; OPEN items for Peter
	docs/DESIGN.md = Envelope format, prior art, and the recorded revocation + key-custody decisions.
	docs/KEY_CEREMONY_V1.md = Ceremony runbook: shortest path to the Oct 15 beta, Peter's exact actions, restore assurance, production positive control, expiry dry-run, milestones
	docs/KEY_PROVIDERS.md = Provider boundary, encrypted-keyfile adapter, honest unavailable states, and deferred owner/hardware gates
	docs/KEY_REGISTRY.md = Public key registry: production roles (pending ceremony) and test roles with .pub hashes
	docs/LICENSING_PRIOR_ART.md = Survey of license-enforcement prior art (serials, signed files, activation, dongles, receipts, DRM) and the Mecha decisions it informs
	docs/MECHA_LICENSE_CONTRACT_V1.md = DRAFT shared licensing contract sigil leads for validate/validate_gui/entropy_shield/mecha-commerce: frozen payload+expiry rules, proposed policy module, trust roles, acceptance vectors, redteam boundaries
	docs/RELEASE_GATES.md = Canonical licensing release gates: pin-specific closed evidence (Linux x86_64 only), owner-assigned open items, and the per-candidate/per-platform revalidation every release must re-earn
	docs/UPDATE_SIGNING_CONTRACT_V1.md = Update signing contract: domain separation, verify-before-parse manifest rules, (sequence, payload sha256) anti-rollback, delta trust shapes, update-key rotation/compromise limits, gaps and questions
	examples/demo = DEMO keypair + signed license (release-plan JSON payload) — dev-only fixtures for integrators and the conformance suite; passphrase 'demo-not-for-production'
	examples/embed_minimal.c = Smallest useful embedder (verify license, print payload) — compiled with stock cc and run with tamper control by tests/test_c_conformance
	examples/hint_vectors = Device-hint KATs and rejects (contract 15.1, mecha-hint-vectors/1), hashed by coreutils; oracle for mecha_policy hintHash
	examples/install_cert_vectors = Installation-certificate test vectors (contract §15): test-install-cert key, signed certs, coreutils machine-hash KATs, expected-decision manifest
	examples/license_vectors = License-class fixture matrix: test-beta/test-paid TEST-ONLY keypairs, 9 signed vectors (valid/expired/boundary/clamp/leap/wrong-product/wrong-class/malformed-expiry), manifest.json = mecha_policy TDD spec, regenerable via ./generate
	examples/license_vectors/README.md = What each test-trust artifact is; PKCS#8 seeds exist for WebCrypto issuers, derived offline, no seed-export command in sigil
	examples/renewal_vectors = Offline-renewal request and bundle vectors (contract §14.3), canonical jq -cS JSON embedding existing signed envelopes
	examples/renewal_vectors/bundle_cert_displaced.json = Bundle with optional unsigned displaced {first_activated} (contract 15.2); equals bundle_cert_only minus displaced
	examples/renewal_vectors/request_activate_hints.json = Renewal request with optional hints object (contract 14.3 + 15.1); equals request_activate minus hints
	examples/update_vectors = mecha-update/v1 signed test vectors for validate_gui's updater TDD — test-only keypair, valid + 4 rejection cases, error-class asserted by tests/integration/update_vectors.sh
	include/sigil_sign.h = Header for libsigil_sign.a. NOT for products - they link libsigil.a only.
	mutate = Mutation testing: plants known defects, counts kills. Found the FFI leak-blindness. Allowlist of accepted survivors.
	src/envelope.zig = JSON envelope parse/write + verifyEnvelope: decode printable-binary, verify, only then release payload bytes.
	src/ffi.zig = The C ABI (real public API): every export fn sigil_*, incl. sigil_verify_envelope and sigil_strerror. Static lib root.
	src/ffi_sign.zig = Signing C ABI in a SEPARATE libsigil_sign.a. Only place randomness lives. No secret ever crosses the boundary.
	src/key_provider.zig = Opaque signing port with capability preflight and classified hardware/offline provider states
	src/lib.zig = Importable Zig module root. Re-exports verify + envelope. Emits NO C symbols and needs no libc.
	src/module_probe.zig = Test fixture (not shipped): forces codegen of the importable Zig module so nm can inspect the sanctioned sibling-Zig consumer path.
	src/paper.zig = Paper cold copies: sealed keyfile/hot bundle as QR + 64-col base64 text + identifying text, one page each
	src/pdf.zig = Minimal PDF 1.4 writer: pages of text (standard Type1 fonts, selectable) and filled rectangles; exact xref
	src/qr.zig = Cleanroom QR encoder (byte mode, v1-40, L/M/Q/H): RS over GF(2^8), masks, BCH format/version; PBM debug output
	src/sign.zig = Pure signing and encrypted-keyfile provider #1: owns key unwrap/expansion/signing behind the provider port; never ships
	src/transcript.zig = The signing transcript (domain ‖ alg ‖ u64be len ‖ verbatim payload) — sole encoder for what Ed25519 signs; injectivity/downgrade/domain-separation tests
	src/verify.zig = Ed25519 primitive: verify(payload, sig, pubkey). Pure, std-only, the entire dependency budget of an embedder.
	test = Master suite: Zig unit tests + CLI tests. Exit code = failure count.
	tests/cli/test_cli = Bash CLI surface tests. Never set -e: most cases assert non-zero exits.
	tests/integration/hint_vectors.sh = Hint vectors: byte-identical regeneration, coreutils recompute, input/hint equivalence classes
	tests/integration/install_cert_vectors.sh = Verifies install-cert vectors under their key only, license hashes against real envelopes, machine hashes via coreutils
	tests/integration/license_vectors.sh = Crypto-layer assertions over the license-class vectors: role verification byte-identity, cross-role SIGNATURE-class rejection, manifest consistency, vacuity guards
	tests/integration/renewal_vectors.sh = Checks renewal vectors are canonical, carry exact keys, and embed exact verifiable envelopes
	tests/integration/update_vectors.sh = CI-gated vector suite: purpose boundary (license↔update replay must fail at SIGNATURE), tamper/wrong-key cases, vacuity guards
	tests/test_no_signing_symbols = MFIC control: nm asserts libsigil.a contains no signing code. Verified to fail when violated.
]
